========================================
Harding Standard Library Demo
========================================

=== Numbers ===
10 + 3 = 13
10 - 3 = 7
10 / 3 = 3.3333333333333335
10 // 3 = 3
10 max: 3 = 10
10 min: 3 = 3
10 between: 5 and: 15 = true

=== Strings ===
Original: Hello, World!
Size: 13
Uppercase: HELLO, WORLD!
Lowercase: hello, world!
Trim: spaces
Index of World: 7
Contains Hello: true
Replace: Hello, Harding!
Split:
  Part: a
  Part: b
  Part: c
  Part: d

=== Arrays ===
Array: #(1 2 3)
Size: 3
First: 1
Last: 3
Collect (double each):
  #(2 4 6 8 10)
Select (greater than 3):
  #(4 5 6)
Inject (concatenate):
  Concatenated: abc

=== Tables ===
Name: Alice
Age: 30
Size: 3
Keys:
  city
  age
  name

=== Loops ===
Counting with timesRepeat:
  Hello!
  Hello!
  Hello!
Counting with to:do:
  Count: 1
  Count: 2
  Count: 3
  Count: 4
  Count: 5
While loop:
  While: 0
  While: 1
  While: 2

